From c1593cdaa61e596302f8bbb57204f0d8b86183bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kleeedolinux <71413974+kleeedolinux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:41:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] x86/entry: leave thread_info.status alone on 64-bit syscall
 exit

Every return to user space cleared TS_COMPAT with a read-modify-write,
which dirties the first cacheline of task_struct on each 64-bit syscall.
That line also holds __state, on_cpu and thread_info.cpu, read by wakers
and by mutex owner spinners. Write the field only when a bit is set.

perf c2c, perf bench epoll wait on a 48-core host: 976 of 14741 HITMs
landed on this line before, and it leaves the top lines after. epoll,
pipe, futex and syscall throughput do not change beyond noise.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
---
 arch/x86/include/asm/entry-common.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/x86/include/asm/entry-common.h b/arch/x86/include/asm/entry-common.h
index 3fed46bd968..3d1c56982ef 100644
--- a/arch/x86/include/asm/entry-common.h
+++ b/arch/x86/include/asm/entry-common.h
@@ -78,7 +78,8 @@ static inline void arch_exit_to_user_mode_prepare(struct pt_regs *regs,
 	 * special case only applies after poking regs and before the
 	 * very next return to user mode.
 	 */
-	current_thread_info()->status &= ~(TS_COMPAT | TS_I386_REGS_POKED);
+	if (unlikely(current_thread_info()->status & (TS_COMPAT | TS_I386_REGS_POKED)))
+		current_thread_info()->status &= ~(TS_COMPAT | TS_I386_REGS_POKED);
 #endif
 
 	/* Avoid unnecessary reads of 'x86_ibpb_exit_to_user' */
